window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b213-3504453d4898f9c9.json"]={sha256:"3504453d4898f9c93e3c113877a5b1c2903d022bb0982cec7b30ed05c9e464a3",value:{"id":"b213","title":"阿科松博水壩","titleEn":"Akosombo Dam","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以以阿科松博土石壩廣域湖泊與發電放流界面學習為主線，先用堆石濕陷與水位與合成核心應力轉移界定水力與構造條件，再將共用設備與可用率、廣域湖面與庫容連結到枯水容量與年能量。業主確認壩型與建設年代；公開頁高度長度互有矛盾故不採用，下列工程數值全為教學假設。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops studying Akosombo embankment lake storage and generation-release interfaces through Rockfill wetting and settlement and Synthetic core stress transfer, then connects Shared equipment and availability and Broad lake surface and storage to Drought capacity and annual energy. The owner confirms dam type and construction dates; conflicting published heights and lengths are excluded and all lesson engineering values are hypothetical. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-dams","subcategoryTitle":"世界水壩與水庫","subcategoryTitleEn":"World dams and reservoirs","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-dams","learningTags":["water","water-dams","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["堆石濕陷與水位","Rockfill wetting and settlement"],["反濾過渡與細粒","Filter transitions and fines"],["共用設備與可用率","Shared equipment and availability"],["廣域湖面與庫容","Broad lake surface and storage"],["枯水容量與年能量","Drought capacity and annual energy"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-dam","labels":["堆石濕陷與水位","反濾過渡與細粒","共用設備與可用率","廣域湖面與庫容","枯水容量與年能量"],"labelsEn":["Rockfill wetting and settlement","Filter transitions and fines","Shared equipment and availability","Broad lake surface and storage","Drought capacity and annual energy"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查堆石濕陷與水位：SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m；再獨立檢查合成核心應力轉移：PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa。敏感度：固定淨水頭60m與效率0.9，流量由200增至250m3/s，出力由105.948增至132.435MW；若尾水隨放流上升，實際增加會小於此固定水頭推估。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。業主確認壩型與建設年代；公開頁高度長度互有矛盾故不採用，下列工程數值全為教學假設。 將比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Rockfill wetting and settlement: SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m. Independently examine Synthetic core stress transfer: PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa. Sensitivity: at fixed60m net head and0.9 efficiency, increasing discharge from200 to250m3/s raises output from105.948 to132.435MW. Rising tailwater would reduce the gain relative to this fixed-head estimate. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. The owner confirms dam type and construction dates; conflicting published heights and lengths are excluded and all lesson engineering values are hypothetical. Use the following independent check: Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b213-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「堆石濕陷與水位」與「合成核心應力轉移」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rockfill wetting and settlement\" and \"Synthetic core stress transfer\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b213-v15-01","title":"堆石濕陷與水位：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rockfill wetting and settlement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「堆石濕陷與水位」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rockfill wetting and settlement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"堆石壩蓄水可能改變顆粒接觸與破碎，濕潤後變形需與施工壓實沉陷分開。平均軸向應變乘厚度只估均勻壓縮量，不能代表整壩三維沉陷；應以分區材料試驗與蓄水前後測點反應建立對照，避免只看壩頂總量。 驗證時應比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎，並辨識以下失效情境：濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「堆石濕陷與水位」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wetting can change rockfill contacts and breakage, and its deformation should be separated from construction settlement. Mean axial strain times thickness describes uniform compression only, not the three-dimensional dam. Compare zoned material tests with pre- and postimpoundment markers rather than relying on crest settlement alone. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rockfill wetting and settlement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有蓄水後沉陷都只是施工壓實尚未完成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every postimpoundment settlement merely reflects unfinished construction compaction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「堆石濕陷與水位」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rockfill wetting and settlement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-01-k1","title":"堆石濕陷與水位","titleEn":"Rockfill wetting and settlement","text":"堆石壩蓄水可能改變顆粒接觸與破碎，濕潤後變形需與施工壓實沉陷分開。平均軸向應變乘厚度只估均勻壓縮量，不能代表整壩三維沉陷；應以分區材料試驗與蓄水前後測點反應建立對照，避免只看壩頂總量。","textEn":"Wetting can change rockfill contacts and breakage, and its deformation should be separated from construction settlement. Mean axial strain times thickness describes uniform compression only, not the three-dimensional dam.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有蓄水後沉陷都只是施工壓實尚未完成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every postimpoundment settlement merely reflects unfinished construction compaction Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「堆石濕陷與水位」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rockfill wetting and settlement\" is correct?","options":["所有蓄水後沉陷都只是施工壓實尚未完成","堆石壩蓄水可能改變顆粒接觸與破碎，濕潤後變形需與施工壓實沉陷分開。","平均覆土應力高就保證核心各方向應力都高"],"optionsEn":["Every postimpoundment settlement merely reflects unfinished construction compaction","Wetting can change rockfill contacts and breakage, and its deformation should be separated from construction settlement.","High average overburden guarantees high stress in every core direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"堆石壩蓄水可能改變顆粒接觸與破碎，濕潤後變形需與施工壓實沉陷分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wetting can change rockfill contacts and breakage, and its deformation should be separated from construction settlement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b213-v15-02","title":"堆石濕陷與水位：定量估算","titleEn":"Rockfill wetting and settlement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「堆石濕陷與水位」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rockfill wetting and settlement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「堆石濕陷與水位」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rockfill wetting and settlement\", which statement holds?","options":["總洩量相同就表示所有閘門組合效果相同","裝置容量就是任何水頭下都能維持的出力","原創教學假設：SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m。"],"optionsEn":["Equal total release means every gate combination has the same effect","Nameplate capacity is output that can be maintained at every head","Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b213-v15-03","title":"堆石濕陷與水位：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rockfill wetting and settlement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「堆石濕陷與水位」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rockfill wetting and settlement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「堆石濕陷與水位」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rockfill wetting and settlement\"?","options":["比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","靜水位低於壩頂就保證不會有波浪越頂"],"optionsEn":["Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Still water below the crest guarantees no wave overtopping"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b213-v15-04","title":"堆石濕陷與水位：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rockfill wetting and settlement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「堆石濕陷與水位」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rockfill wetting and settlement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形。診斷時應採取以下查核：比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有蓄水後沉陷都只是施工壓實尚未完成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every postimpoundment settlement merely reflects unfinished construction compaction\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形。診斷時應採取以下查核：比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「堆石濕陷與水位」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rockfill wetting and settlement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形。","平均覆土應力高就保證核心各方向應力都高"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell.","High average overburden guarantees high stress in every core direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b213-v15-05","title":"合成核心應力轉移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Synthetic core stress transfer: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「合成核心應力轉移」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Synthetic core stress transfer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"合成土石壩核心與兩側材料剛度不同時，拱效應可能把部分豎向荷載轉移到較硬區，降低核心局部總應力。單一有效應力差只呈現孔壓餘量，不能直接預報水力劈裂；需評估最小主應力、材料拉伸特性與接觸變形。 驗證時應比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差，並辨識以下失效情境：用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「合成核心應力轉移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In a synthetic zoned dam, stiffness contrast can transfer vertical load away from the core. A scalar effective-stress difference illustrates pressure margin but does not predict hydraulic fracture. Evaluate minimum principal stress, tensile behavior and interface deformation instead of treating average overburden as the complete stress state. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Synthetic core stress transfer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均覆土應力高就保證核心各方向應力都高」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High average overburden guarantees high stress in every core direction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「合成核心應力轉移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Synthetic core stress transfer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-05-k1","title":"合成核心應力轉移","titleEn":"Synthetic core stress transfer","text":"合成土石壩核心與兩側材料剛度不同時，拱效應可能把部分豎向荷載轉移到較硬區，降低核心局部總應力。單一有效應力差只呈現孔壓餘量，不能直接預報水力劈裂；需評估最小主應力、材料拉伸特性與接觸變形。","textEn":"In a synthetic zoned dam, stiffness contrast can transfer vertical load away from the core. A scalar effective-stress difference illustrates pressure margin but does not predict hydraulic fracture.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均覆土應力高就保證核心各方向應力都高 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High average overburden guarantees high stress in every core direction Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「合成核心應力轉移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Synthetic core stress transfer\" is correct?","options":["平均覆土應力高就保證核心各方向應力都高","料場試驗合格就保證每個鋪築界面都合格","合成土石壩核心與兩側材料剛度不同時，拱效應可能把部分豎向荷載轉移到較硬區，降低核心局部總應力。"],"optionsEn":["High average overburden guarantees high stress in every core direction","Passing stockpile tests guarantees every placed interface is acceptable","In a synthetic zoned dam, stiffness contrast can transfer vertical load away from the core."],"answer":2,"explanation":"合成土石壩核心與兩側材料剛度不同時，拱效應可能把部分豎向荷載轉移到較硬區，降低核心局部總應力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In a synthetic zoned dam, stiffness contrast can transfer vertical load away from the core. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b213-v15-06","title":"合成核心應力轉移：定量估算","titleEn":"Synthetic core stress transfer: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「合成核心應力轉移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Synthetic core stress transfer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「合成核心應力轉移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Synthetic core stress transfer\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa。","閘門數量多就保證沒有任何共同失效點","湖面積一旦量過就能固定用於所有水位"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa.","A large number of gates guarantees no common failure point","One measured lake area applies unchanged at every stage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b213-v15-07","title":"合成核心應力轉移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Synthetic core stress transfer: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「合成核心應力轉移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Synthetic core stress transfer” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「合成核心應力轉移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Synthetic core stress transfer\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差。","每天總放流量相同就表示下游影響完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones.","Equal daily release volume guarantees identical downstream effects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b213-v15-08","title":"合成核心應力轉移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Synthetic core stress transfer: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「合成核心應力轉移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Synthetic core stress transfer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均覆土應力高就保證核心各方向應力都高」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High average overburden guarantees high stress in every core direction\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「合成核心應力轉移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Synthetic core stress transfer\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","料場試驗合格就保證每個鋪築界面都合格","用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Passing stockpile tests guarantees every placed interface is acceptable","Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b213-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「反濾過渡與細粒」與「分孔洩流與不均流」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Filter transitions and fines\" and \"Multiple bays and uneven discharge\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b213-v15-09","title":"反濾過渡與細粒：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Filter transitions and fines: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「反濾過渡與細粒」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Filter transitions and fines” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"堆石與細粒防滲材料之間需要連續過渡，否則粒徑反差可能讓細土移入大孔隙。示意粒徑比只供辨認幾何尺度，不是所有土類的核准準則；材料分離、施工污染及交界厚度都須以分區取樣與試驗確認。 驗證時應於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度，並辨識以下失效情境：只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「反濾過渡與細粒」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Transitions between rockfill and fine barrier material must remain continuous to prevent fines entering large pores. An illustrative grain-size ratio identifies scale but does not approve every soil type. Verify segregation, contamination and interface thickness through zoned sampling and applicable material tests. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Filter transitions and fines” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：SyntheticTransitionD15=0.8 mm; protectedSoild85=0.25 mm; ratio=0.8/0.25=3.2 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticTransitionD15=0.8 mm; protectedSoild85=0.25 mm; ratio=0.8/0.25=3.2 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「料場試驗合格就保證每個鋪築界面都合格」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing stockpile tests guarantees every placed interface is acceptable\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「反濾過渡與細粒」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Filter transitions and fines”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-09-k1","title":"反濾過渡與細粒","titleEn":"Filter transitions and fines","text":"堆石與細粒防滲材料之間需要連續過渡，否則粒徑反差可能讓細土移入大孔隙。示意粒徑比只供辨認幾何尺度，不是所有土類的核准準則；材料分離、施工污染及交界厚度都須以分區取樣與試驗確認。","textEn":"Transitions between rockfill and fine barrier material must remain continuous to prevent fines entering large pores. An illustrative grain-size ratio identifies scale but does not approve every soil type.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：料場試驗合格就保證每個鋪築界面都合格 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing stockpile tests guarantees every placed interface is acceptable Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「反濾過渡與細粒」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Filter transitions and fines\" is correct?","options":["堆石與細粒防滲材料之間需要連續過渡，否則粒徑反差可能讓細土移入大孔隙。","料場試驗合格就保證每個鋪築界面都合格","總洩量相同就表示所有閘門組合效果相同"],"optionsEn":["Transitions between rockfill and fine barrier material must remain continuous to prevent fines entering large pores.","Passing stockpile tests guarantees every placed interface is acceptable","Equal total release means every gate combination has the same effect"],"answer":0,"explanation":"堆石與細粒防滲材料之間需要連續過渡，否則粒徑反差可能讓細土移入大孔隙。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Transitions between rockfill and fine barrier material must remain continuous to prevent fines entering large pores. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b213-v15-10","title":"反濾過渡與細粒：定量估算","titleEn":"Filter transitions and fines: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「反濾過渡與細粒」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Filter transitions and fines” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：SyntheticTransitionD15=0.8 mm; protectedSoild85=0.25 mm; ratio=0.8/0.25=3.2 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticTransitionD15=0.8 mm; protectedSoild85=0.25 mm; ratio=0.8/0.25=3.2 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：SyntheticTransitionD15=0.8 mm; protectedSoild85=0.25 mm; ratio=0.8/0.25=3.2 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticTransitionD15=0.8 mm; protectedSoild85=0.25 mm; ratio=0.8/0.25=3.2 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「反濾過渡與細粒」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Filter transitions and fines\", which statement holds?","options":["裝置容量就是任何水頭下都能維持的出力","原創教學假設：SyntheticTransitionD15=0.8 mm; protectedSoild85=0.25 mm; ratio=0.8/0.25=3.2 dimensionless。","靜水位低於壩頂就保證不會有波浪越頂"],"optionsEn":["Nameplate capacity is output that can be maintained at every head","Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticTransitionD15=0.8 mm; protectedSoild85=0.25 mm; ratio=0.8/0.25=3.2 dimensionless.","Still water below the crest guarantees no wave overtopping"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：SyntheticTransitionD15=0.8 mm; protectedSoild85=0.25 mm; ratio=0.8/0.25=3.2 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticTransitionD15=0.8 mm; protectedSoild85=0.25 mm; ratio=0.8/0.25=3.2 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b213-v15-11","title":"反濾過渡與細粒：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Filter transitions and fines: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「反濾過渡與細粒」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Filter transitions and fines” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「反濾過渡與細粒」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Filter transitions and fines\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","容量因數降低就必定代表水輪機效率降低","於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A lower capacity factor necessarily means lower turbine efficiency","Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b213-v15-12","title":"反濾過渡與細粒：失效診斷","titleEn":"Filter transitions and fines: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「反濾過渡與細粒」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Filter transitions and fines” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離。診斷時應採取以下查核：於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement. Diagnose it by the following check: Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「料場試驗合格就保證每個鋪築界面都合格」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing stockpile tests guarantees every placed interface is acceptable\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離。診斷時應採取以下查核：於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement. Diagnose it by the following check: Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「反濾過渡與細粒」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Filter transitions and fines\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","總洩量相同就表示所有閘門組合效果相同"],"optionsEn":["Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Equal total release means every gate combination has the same effect"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b213-v15-13","title":"分孔洩流與不均流：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Multiple bays and uneven discharge: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「分孔洩流與不均流」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Multiple bays and uneven discharge” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多孔溢洪道的總流量由各孔實際開度與水頭決定，孔數平均不代表局部水舌或下游壓力相同。合成各孔流量加總只是水量帳；閘門組合改變可能使相鄰水舌交互作用，須對照下游消能與岸坡反應。 驗證時應同步記錄各孔開度與下游水舌位置並核對總流量，並辨識以下失效情境：相同總洩量的不同孔組合可能集中衝擊單側岸坡。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分孔洩流與不均流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Total spillway flow sums actual bay discharges, not an assumed uniform share. Adding synthetic bay flows is only mass accounting. Different combinations can alter jet interaction and downstream pressure, so check dissipation and bank response alongside opening and head at each bay. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Record bay openings and downstream jet positions together and check total flow. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Different bay combinations at equal total flow can concentrate impact on one bank. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Multiple bays and uneven discharge” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Three hypothetical bays discharge=120,100,80 m3/s; totalQ=120+100+80=300 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Three hypothetical bays discharge=120,100,80 m3/s; totalQ=120+100+80=300 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「總洩量相同就表示所有閘門組合效果相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal total release means every gate combination has the same effect\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分孔洩流與不均流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Multiple bays and uneven discharge”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-13-k1","title":"分孔洩流與不均流","titleEn":"Multiple bays and uneven discharge","text":"多孔溢洪道的總流量由各孔實際開度與水頭決定，孔數平均不代表局部水舌或下游壓力相同。合成各孔流量加總只是水量帳；閘門組合改變可能使相鄰水舌交互作用，須對照下游消能與岸坡反應。","textEn":"Total spillway flow sums actual bay discharges, not an assumed uniform share. Adding synthetic bay flows is only mass accounting.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總洩量相同就表示所有閘門組合效果相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal total release means every gate combination has the same effect Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分孔洩流與不均流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Multiple bays and uneven discharge\" is correct?","options":["總洩量相同就表示所有閘門組合效果相同","多孔溢洪道的總流量由各孔實際開度與水頭決定，孔數平均不代表局部水舌或下游壓力相同。","閘門數量多就保證沒有任何共同失效點"],"optionsEn":["Equal total release means every gate combination has the same effect","Total spillway flow sums actual bay discharges, not an assumed uniform share.","A large number of gates guarantees no common failure point"],"answer":1,"explanation":"多孔溢洪道的總流量由各孔實際開度與水頭決定，孔數平均不代表局部水舌或下游壓力相同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Total spillway flow sums actual bay discharges, not an assumed uniform share. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b213-v15-14","title":"分孔洩流與不均流：定量估算","titleEn":"Multiple bays and uneven discharge: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分孔洩流與不均流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Multiple bays and uneven discharge” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Three hypothetical bays discharge=120,100,80 m3/s; totalQ=120+100+80=300 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Three hypothetical bays discharge=120,100,80 m3/s; totalQ=120+100+80=300 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記錄各孔開度與下游水舌位置並核對總流量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record bay openings and downstream jet positions together and check total flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Three hypothetical bays discharge=120,100,80 m3/s; totalQ=120+100+80=300 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Three hypothetical bays discharge=120,100,80 m3/s; totalQ=120+100+80=300 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分孔洩流與不均流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Multiple bays and uneven discharge\", which statement holds?","options":["湖面積一旦量過就能固定用於所有水位","每天總放流量相同就表示下游影響完全相同","原創教學假設：Three hypothetical bays discharge=120,100,80 m3/s; totalQ=120+100+80=300 m3/s。"],"optionsEn":["One measured lake area applies unchanged at every stage","Equal daily release volume guarantees identical downstream effects","Original teaching assumptions: Three hypothetical bays discharge=120,100,80 m3/s; totalQ=120+100+80=300 m3/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Three hypothetical bays discharge=120,100,80 m3/s; totalQ=120+100+80=300 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Three hypothetical bays discharge=120,100,80 m3/s; totalQ=120+100+80=300 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b213-v15-15","title":"分孔洩流與不均流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Multiple bays and uneven discharge: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分孔洩流與不均流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Multiple bays and uneven discharge” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記錄各孔開度與下游水舌位置並核對總流量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「相同總洩量的不同孔組合可能集中衝擊單側岸坡」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record bay openings and downstream jet positions together and check total flow. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Different bay combinations at equal total flow can concentrate impact on one bank. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步記錄各孔開度與下游水舌位置並核對總流量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對相同總洩量的不同孔組合可能集中衝擊單側岸坡，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Record bay openings and downstream jet positions together and check total flow. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Different bay combinations at equal total flow can concentrate impact on one bank. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：相同總洩量的不同孔組合可能集中衝擊單側岸坡。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Different bay combinations at equal total flow can concentrate impact on one bank. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記錄各孔開度與下游水舌位置並核對總流量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「相同總洩量的不同孔組合可能集中衝擊單側岸坡」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Record bay openings and downstream jet positions together and check total flow. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Different bay combinations at equal total flow can concentrate impact on one bank. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步記錄各孔開度與下游水舌位置並核對總流量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對相同總洩量的不同孔組合可能集中衝擊單側岸坡，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Record bay openings and downstream jet positions together and check total flow. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Different bay combinations at equal total flow can concentrate impact on one bank. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分孔洩流與不均流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Multiple bays and uneven discharge\"?","options":["同步記錄各孔開度與下游水舌位置並核對總流量。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","所有蓄水後沉陷都只是施工壓實尚未完成"],"optionsEn":["Record bay openings and downstream jet positions together and check total flow.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Every postimpoundment settlement merely reflects unfinished construction compaction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步記錄各孔開度與下游水舌位置並核對總流量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record bay openings and downstream jet positions together and check total flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b213-v15-16","title":"分孔洩流與不均流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Multiple bays and uneven discharge: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分孔洩流與不均流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Multiple bays and uneven discharge” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"相同總洩量的不同孔組合可能集中衝擊單側岸坡。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步記錄各孔開度與下游水舌位置並核對總流量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Different bay combinations at equal total flow can concentrate impact on one bank. Diagnose it by the following check: Record bay openings and downstream jet positions together and check total flow. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總洩量相同就表示所有閘門組合效果相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal total release means every gate combination has the same effect\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"相同總洩量的不同孔組合可能集中衝擊單側岸坡。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步記錄各孔開度與下游水舌位置並核對總流量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Different bay combinations at equal total flow can concentrate impact on one bank. Diagnose it by the following check: Record bay openings and downstream jet positions together and check total flow. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分孔洩流與不均流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Multiple bays and uneven discharge\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","相同總洩量的不同孔組合可能集中衝擊單側岸坡。","閘門數量多就保證沒有任何共同失效點"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Different bay combinations at equal total flow can concentrate impact on one bank.","A large number of gates guarantees no common failure point"],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同總洩量的不同孔組合可能集中衝擊單側岸坡。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Different bay combinations at equal total flow can concentrate impact on one bank. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b213-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「共用設備與可用率」與「機組出力與水頭」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shared equipment and availability\" and \"Generating output and hydraulic head\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b213-v15-17","title":"共用設備與可用率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared equipment and availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「共用設備與可用率」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shared equipment and availability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"共用啟閉設備使多個閘門在維修與故障時具有共同依賴，不能把各孔當完全獨立備援。串聯可用率乘積僅適用獨立失效及簡化狀態，現場共因故障需另建事件樹；應檢查設備移動時間、停機及替代方案。 驗證時應以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力，並辨識以下失效情境：共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「共用設備與可用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shared hoisting equipment creates common dependencies among gates. Multiplying availabilities represents an ideal independent series system only; common-cause failures require another model. Examine movement time, outages and alternatives instead of counting every gate as fully independent redundancy merely because the leaves are separate. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Shared equipment and availability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「閘門數量多就保證沒有任何共同失效點」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A large number of gates guarantees no common failure point\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「共用設備與可用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Shared equipment and availability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-17-k1","title":"共用設備與可用率","titleEn":"Shared equipment and availability","text":"共用啟閉設備使多個閘門在維修與故障時具有共同依賴，不能把各孔當完全獨立備援。串聯可用率乘積僅適用獨立失效及簡化狀態，現場共因故障需另建事件樹；應檢查設備移動時間、停機及替代方案。","textEn":"Shared hoisting equipment creates common dependencies among gates. Multiplying availabilities represents an ideal independent series system only; common-cause failures require another model.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：閘門數量多就保證沒有任何共同失效點 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A large number of gates guarantees no common failure point Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共用設備與可用率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared equipment and availability\" is correct?","options":["閘門數量多就保證沒有任何共同失效點","裝置容量就是任何水頭下都能維持的出力","共用啟閉設備使多個閘門在維修與故障時具有共同依賴，不能把各孔當完全獨立備援。"],"optionsEn":["A large number of gates guarantees no common failure point","Nameplate capacity is output that can be maintained at every head","Shared hoisting equipment creates common dependencies among gates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共用啟閉設備使多個閘門在維修與故障時具有共同依賴，不能把各孔當完全獨立備援。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shared hoisting equipment creates common dependencies among gates. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b213-v15-18","title":"共用設備與可用率：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared equipment and availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「共用設備與可用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shared equipment and availability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共用設備與可用率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared equipment and availability\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless。","靜水位低於壩頂就保證不會有波浪越頂","容量因數降低就必定代表水輪機效率降低"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless.","Still water below the crest guarantees no wave overtopping","A lower capacity factor necessarily means lower turbine efficiency"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b213-v15-19","title":"共用設備與可用率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared equipment and availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「共用設備與可用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shared equipment and availability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共用設備與可用率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared equipment and availability\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力。","平均覆土應力高就保證核心各方向應力都高"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation.","High average overburden guarantees high stress in every core direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b213-v15-20","title":"共用設備與可用率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared equipment and availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「共用設備與可用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shared equipment and availability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門。診斷時應採取以下查核：以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates. Diagnose it by the following check: Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「閘門數量多就保證沒有任何共同失效點」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A large number of gates guarantees no common failure point\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門。診斷時應採取以下查核：以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates. Diagnose it by the following check: Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共用設備與可用率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared equipment and availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","裝置容量就是任何水頭下都能維持的出力","共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Nameplate capacity is output that can be maintained at every head","A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b213-v15-21","title":"機組出力與水頭：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Generating output and hydraulic head: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「機組出力與水頭」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Generating output and hydraulic head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"阿科松博提供水庫發電與放流協調的案例，機組出力需用淨水頭而不是壩高。尾水與進水損失會隨流量改變，效率也受工作點影響；合成定效率算例只是能量量級，不能以裝置容量倒推出未量測的流量。 驗證時應以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍，並辨識以下失效情境：用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「機組出力與水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Akosombo provides context for coordinated reservoir generation and releases. Output uses net head rather than dam height; tailwater, losses and efficiency vary with operating point. A constant-efficiency illustration gives an energy scale and does not justify recovering unmeasured flow directly from nameplate capacity. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Generating output and hydraulic head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW.","failure":"常見誤解：「裝置容量就是任何水頭下都能維持的出力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Nameplate capacity is output that can be maintained at every head\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「機組出力與水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Generating output and hydraulic head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-21-k1","title":"機組出力與水頭","titleEn":"Generating output and hydraulic head","text":"阿科松博提供水庫發電與放流協調的案例，機組出力需用淨水頭而不是壩高。尾水與進水損失會隨流量改變，效率也受工作點影響；合成定效率算例只是能量量級，不能以裝置容量倒推出未量測的流量。","textEn":"Akosombo provides context for coordinated reservoir generation and releases. Output uses net head rather than dam height; tailwater, losses and efficiency vary with operating point.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裝置容量就是任何水頭下都能維持的出力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Nameplate capacity is output that can be maintained at every head Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「機組出力與水頭」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Generating output and hydraulic head\" is correct?","options":["阿科松博提供水庫發電與放流協調的案例，機組出力需用淨水頭而不是壩高。","裝置容量就是任何水頭下都能維持的出力","湖面積一旦量過就能固定用於所有水位"],"optionsEn":["Akosombo provides context for coordinated reservoir generation and releases.","Nameplate capacity is output that can be maintained at every head","One measured lake area applies unchanged at every stage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"阿科松博提供水庫發電與放流協調的案例，機組出力需用淨水頭而不是壩高。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Akosombo provides context for coordinated reservoir generation and releases. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b213-v15-22","title":"機組出力與水頭：定量估算","titleEn":"Generating output and hydraulic head: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「機組出力與水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Generating output and hydraulic head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「機組出力與水頭」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Generating output and hydraulic head\", which statement holds?","options":["每天總放流量相同就表示下游影響完全相同","原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW。","所有蓄水後沉陷都只是施工壓實尚未完成"],"optionsEn":["Equal daily release volume guarantees identical downstream effects","Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW.","Every postimpoundment settlement merely reflects unfinished construction compaction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b213-v15-23","title":"機組出力與水頭：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Generating output and hydraulic head: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「機組出力與水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Generating output and hydraulic head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「機組出力與水頭」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Generating output and hydraulic head\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","料場試驗合格就保證每個鋪築界面都合格","以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Passing stockpile tests guarantees every placed interface is acceptable","Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b213-v15-24","title":"機組出力與水頭：失效診斷","titleEn":"Generating output and hydraulic head: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「機組出力與水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Generating output and hydraulic head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量。診斷時應採取以下查核：以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. Diagnose it by the following check: Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裝置容量就是任何水頭下都能維持的出力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Nameplate capacity is output that can be maintained at every head\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量。診斷時應採取以下查核：以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. Diagnose it by the following check: Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「機組出力與水頭」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Generating output and hydraulic head\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","湖面積一旦量過就能固定用於所有水位"],"optionsEn":["Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","One measured lake area applies unchanged at every stage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b213-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「廣域湖面與庫容」與「風浪水位與壩頂」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Broad lake surface and storage\" and \"Wind setup and crest checks\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b213-v15-25","title":"廣域湖面與庫容：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Broad lake surface and storage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「廣域湖面與庫容」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Broad lake surface and storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大面積湖泊的小幅水位變化可能對應大量庫容，但面積並非固定，岸線地形使水位容量關係非線性。以定面積近似只適用短範圍示意，應使用實測地形更新曲線；不同高程基準不能直接拼接成容量變化。 驗證時應以分水位面積曲線與重複測深核對局部容量斜率，並辨識以下失效情境：固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「廣域湖面與庫容」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A small level change over a broad lake can represent substantial storage, but shoreline geometry makes area variable. A constant-area approximation covers a limited range only. Update the relation from bathymetry and keep vertical datums consistent rather than joining unlike surveys into a storage trend. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Broad lake surface and storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：HypotheticalMeanArea=1000 km2; stageChange=0.20 m; localStorageChange=1000e6*0.20/1e6=200 million m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalMeanArea=1000 km2; stageChange=0.20 m; localStorageChange=1000e6*0.20/1e6=200 million m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「湖面積一旦量過就能固定用於所有水位」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One measured lake area applies unchanged at every stage\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「廣域湖面與庫容」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Broad lake surface and storage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-25-k1","title":"廣域湖面與庫容","titleEn":"Broad lake surface and storage","text":"大面積湖泊的小幅水位變化可能對應大量庫容，但面積並非固定，岸線地形使水位容量關係非線性。以定面積近似只適用短範圍示意，應使用實測地形更新曲線；不同高程基準不能直接拼接成容量變化。","textEn":"A small level change over a broad lake can represent substantial storage, but shoreline geometry makes area variable. A constant-area approximation covers a limited range only.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：湖面積一旦量過就能固定用於所有水位 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One measured lake area applies unchanged at every stage Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「廣域湖面與庫容」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Broad lake surface and storage\" is correct?","options":["湖面積一旦量過就能固定用於所有水位","大面積湖泊的小幅水位變化可能對應大量庫容，但面積並非固定，岸線地形使水位容量關係非線性。","靜水位低於壩頂就保證不會有波浪越頂"],"optionsEn":["One measured lake area applies unchanged at every stage","A small level change over a broad lake can represent substantial storage, but shoreline geometry makes area variable.","Still water below the crest guarantees no wave overtopping"],"answer":1,"explanation":"大面積湖泊的小幅水位變化可能對應大量庫容，但面積並非固定，岸線地形使水位容量關係非線性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A small level change over a broad lake can represent substantial storage, but shoreline geometry makes area variable. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b213-v15-26","title":"廣域湖面與庫容：定量估算","titleEn":"Broad lake surface and storage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「廣域湖面與庫容」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Broad lake surface and storage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：HypotheticalMeanArea=1000 km2; stageChange=0.20 m; localStorageChange=1000e6*0.20/1e6=200 million m3。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalMeanArea=1000 km2; stageChange=0.20 m; localStorageChange=1000e6*0.20/1e6=200 million m3. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以分水位面積曲線與重複測深核對局部容量斜率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：HypotheticalMeanArea=1000 km2; stageChange=0.20 m; localStorageChange=1000e6*0.20/1e6=200 million m3。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalMeanArea=1000 km2; stageChange=0.20 m; localStorageChange=1000e6*0.20/1e6=200 million m3. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「廣域湖面與庫容」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Broad lake surface and storage\", which statement holds?","options":["容量因數降低就必定代表水輪機效率降低","平均覆土應力高就保證核心各方向應力都高","原創教學假設：HypotheticalMeanArea=1000 km2; stageChange=0.20 m; localStorageChange=1000e6*0.20/1e6=200 million m3。"],"optionsEn":["A lower capacity factor necessarily means lower turbine efficiency","High average overburden guarantees high stress in every core direction","Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalMeanArea=1000 km2; stageChange=0.20 m; localStorageChange=1000e6*0.20/1e6=200 million m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：HypotheticalMeanArea=1000 km2; stageChange=0.20 m; localStorageChange=1000e6*0.20/1e6=200 million m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalMeanArea=1000 km2; stageChange=0.20 m; localStorageChange=1000e6*0.20/1e6=200 million m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b213-v15-27","title":"廣域湖面與庫容：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Broad lake surface and storage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「廣域湖面與庫容」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Broad lake surface and storage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以分水位面積曲線與重複測深核對局部容量斜率。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以分水位面積曲線與重複測深核對局部容量斜率作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以分水位面積曲線與重複測深核對局部容量斜率。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以分水位面積曲線與重複測深核對局部容量斜率作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「廣域湖面與庫容」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Broad lake surface and storage\"?","options":["以分水位面積曲線與重複測深核對局部容量斜率。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","總洩量相同就表示所有閘門組合效果相同"],"optionsEn":["Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Equal total release means every gate combination has the same effect"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以分水位面積曲線與重複測深核對局部容量斜率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b213-v15-28","title":"廣域湖面與庫容：失效診斷","titleEn":"Broad lake surface and storage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「廣域湖面與庫容」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Broad lake surface and storage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容。診斷時應採取以下查核：以分水位面積曲線與重複測深核對局部容量斜率，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. Diagnose it by the following check: Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「湖面積一旦量過就能固定用於所有水位」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One measured lake area applies unchanged at every stage\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容。診斷時應採取以下查核：以分水位面積曲線與重複測深核對局部容量斜率，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. Diagnose it by the following check: Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「廣域湖面與庫容」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Broad lake surface and storage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容。","靜水位低於壩頂就保證不會有波浪越頂"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage.","Still water below the crest guarantees no wave overtopping"],"answer":1,"explanation":"固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b213-v15-29","title":"風浪水位與壩頂：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wind setup and crest checks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「風浪水位與壩頂」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wind setup and crest checks” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"廣域湖泊的風作用可能造成平均水位壅高與短時波浪，兩者應分開並與壩頂高程比較。簡化淨餘高只是已指定工況的幾何帳，不能替代波浪爬升或可靠度分析；還需考慮沉陷、浪向與岸形聚焦。 驗證時應比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向，並辨識以下失效情境：忽略壩頂長期沉陷會高估剩餘餘高。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風浪水位與壩頂」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wind over a broad lake can produce both setup and waves, which must be distinguished in crest checks. A geometric clearance calculation applies to a prescribed case and does not replace runup or reliability analysis. Settlement, direction and shoreline focusing also affect local conditions. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Ignoring long-term crest settlement overstates remaining freeboard. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wind setup and crest checks” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：crestElevation=102 m; stillWater=99 m; setup=0.3 m; prescribedRunup=1.2 m; clearance=102-99-0.3-1.2=1.5 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: crestElevation=102 m; stillWater=99 m; setup=0.3 m; prescribedRunup=1.2 m; clearance=102-99-0.3-1.2=1.5 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「靜水位低於壩頂就保證不會有波浪越頂」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Still water below the crest guarantees no wave overtopping\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風浪水位與壩頂」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wind setup and crest checks”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-29-k1","title":"風浪水位與壩頂","titleEn":"Wind setup and crest checks","text":"廣域湖泊的風作用可能造成平均水位壅高與短時波浪，兩者應分開並與壩頂高程比較。簡化淨餘高只是已指定工況的幾何帳，不能替代波浪爬升或可靠度分析；還需考慮沉陷、浪向與岸形聚焦。","textEn":"Wind over a broad lake can produce both setup and waves, which must be distinguished in crest checks. A geometric clearance calculation applies to a prescribed case and does not replace runup or reliability analysis.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：靜水位低於壩頂就保證不會有波浪越頂 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Still water below the crest guarantees no wave overtopping Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「風浪水位與壩頂」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wind setup and crest checks\" is correct?","options":["靜水位低於壩頂就保證不會有波浪越頂","每天總放流量相同就表示下游影響完全相同","廣域湖泊的風作用可能造成平均水位壅高與短時波浪，兩者應分開並與壩頂高程比較。"],"optionsEn":["Still water below the crest guarantees no wave overtopping","Equal daily release volume guarantees identical downstream effects","Wind over a broad lake can produce both setup and waves, which must be distinguished in crest checks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"廣域湖泊的風作用可能造成平均水位壅高與短時波浪，兩者應分開並與壩頂高程比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wind over a broad lake can produce both setup and waves, which must be distinguished in crest checks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b213-v15-30","title":"風浪水位與壩頂：定量估算","titleEn":"Wind setup and crest checks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風浪水位與壩頂」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wind setup and crest checks” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：crestElevation=102 m; stillWater=99 m; setup=0.3 m; prescribedRunup=1.2 m; clearance=102-99-0.3-1.2=1.5 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: crestElevation=102 m; stillWater=99 m; setup=0.3 m; prescribedRunup=1.2 m; clearance=102-99-0.3-1.2=1.5 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：crestElevation=102 m; stillWater=99 m; setup=0.3 m; prescribedRunup=1.2 m; clearance=102-99-0.3-1.2=1.5 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: crestElevation=102 m; stillWater=99 m; setup=0.3 m; prescribedRunup=1.2 m; clearance=102-99-0.3-1.2=1.5 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「風浪水位與壩頂」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wind setup and crest checks\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：crestElevation=102 m; stillWater=99 m; setup=0.3 m; prescribedRunup=1.2 m; clearance=102-99-0.3-1.2=1.5 m。","所有蓄水後沉陷都只是施工壓實尚未完成","料場試驗合格就保證每個鋪築界面都合格"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: crestElevation=102 m; stillWater=99 m; setup=0.3 m; prescribedRunup=1.2 m; clearance=102-99-0.3-1.2=1.5 m.","Every postimpoundment settlement merely reflects unfinished construction compaction","Passing stockpile tests guarantees every placed interface is acceptable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：crestElevation=102 m; stillWater=99 m; setup=0.3 m; prescribedRunup=1.2 m; clearance=102-99-0.3-1.2=1.5 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: crestElevation=102 m; stillWater=99 m; setup=0.3 m; prescribedRunup=1.2 m; clearance=102-99-0.3-1.2=1.5 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b213-v15-31","title":"風浪水位與壩頂：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wind setup and crest checks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風浪水位與壩頂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wind setup and crest checks” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略壩頂長期沉陷會高估剩餘餘高」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring long-term crest settlement overstates remaining freeboard. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略壩頂長期沉陷會高估剩餘餘高，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring long-term crest settlement overstates remaining freeboard. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略壩頂長期沉陷會高估剩餘餘高。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring long-term crest settlement overstates remaining freeboard. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略壩頂長期沉陷會高估剩餘餘高」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring long-term crest settlement overstates remaining freeboard. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略壩頂長期沉陷會高估剩餘餘高，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring long-term crest settlement overstates remaining freeboard. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「風浪水位與壩頂」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wind setup and crest checks\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向。","閘門數量多就保證沒有任何共同失效點"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction.","A large number of gates guarantees no common failure point"],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b213-v15-32","title":"風浪水位與壩頂：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wind setup and crest checks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風浪水位與壩頂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wind setup and crest checks” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略壩頂長期沉陷會高估剩餘餘高。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring long-term crest settlement overstates remaining freeboard. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「靜水位低於壩頂就保證不會有波浪越頂」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Still water below the crest guarantees no wave overtopping\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略壩頂長期沉陷會高估剩餘餘高。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較壩前水位波浪紀錄與壩頂沉陷並標明浪向，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Ignoring long-term crest settlement overstates remaining freeboard. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare near-dam water levels and waves with crest settlement and wave direction. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「風浪水位與壩頂」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wind setup and crest checks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","每天總放流量相同就表示下游影響完全相同","忽略壩頂長期沉陷會高估剩餘餘高。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal daily release volume guarantees identical downstream effects","Ignoring long-term crest settlement overstates remaining freeboard."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略壩頂長期沉陷會高估剩餘餘高。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring long-term crest settlement overstates remaining freeboard. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b213-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「下游流量爬升」與「枯水容量與年能量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Downstream discharge ramping\" and \"Drought capacity and annual energy\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b213-v15-33","title":"下游流量爬升：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Downstream discharge ramping: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「下游流量爬升」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Downstream discharge ramping” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"發電調峰會改變下游放流時序，平均日水量相同仍可能造成不同水位變化速度。流量差除時間只是放流變率，不能直接等同下游任一斷面的水位升速；河道儲水、傳播時間與支流入流需用路由與量測評估。 驗證時應同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲，並辨識以下失效情境：把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「下游流量爬升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Peaking changes release timing even when daily volume is unchanged. Discharge change divided by time is a release ramp, not the water-level rise at every downstream section. Channel storage, travel time and tributaries require routing and observations to determine actual downstream response. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Downstream discharge ramping” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：ReleaseChangesFrom=100 to220 m3/s over30 min; meanDischargeRamp=(220-100)/30=4 m3/s per min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: ReleaseChangesFrom=100 to220 m3/s over30 min; meanDischargeRamp=(220-100)/30=4 m3/s per min.","failure":"常見誤解：「每天總放流量相同就表示下游影響完全相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal daily release volume guarantees identical downstream effects\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「下游流量爬升」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Downstream discharge ramping”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-33-k1","title":"下游流量爬升","titleEn":"Downstream discharge ramping","text":"發電調峰會改變下游放流時序，平均日水量相同仍可能造成不同水位變化速度。流量差除時間只是放流變率，不能直接等同下游任一斷面的水位升速；河道儲水、傳播時間與支流入流需用路由與量測評估。","textEn":"Peaking changes release timing even when daily volume is unchanged. Discharge change divided by time is a release ramp, not the water-level rise at every downstream section.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每天總放流量相同就表示下游影響完全相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal daily release volume guarantees identical downstream effects Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「下游流量爬升」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Downstream discharge ramping\" is correct?","options":["發電調峰會改變下游放流時序，平均日水量相同仍可能造成不同水位變化速度。","每天總放流量相同就表示下游影響完全相同","容量因數降低就必定代表水輪機效率降低"],"optionsEn":["Peaking changes release timing even when daily volume is unchanged.","Equal daily release volume guarantees identical downstream effects","A lower capacity factor necessarily means lower turbine efficiency"],"answer":0,"explanation":"發電調峰會改變下游放流時序，平均日水量相同仍可能造成不同水位變化速度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Peaking changes release timing even when daily volume is unchanged. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b213-v15-34","title":"下游流量爬升：定量估算","titleEn":"Downstream discharge ramping: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「下游流量爬升」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Downstream discharge ramping” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：ReleaseChangesFrom=100 to220 m3/s over30 min; meanDischargeRamp=(220-100)/30=4 m3/s per min。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: ReleaseChangesFrom=100 to220 m3/s over30 min; meanDischargeRamp=(220-100)/30=4 m3/s per min. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：ReleaseChangesFrom=100 to220 m3/s over30 min; meanDischargeRamp=(220-100)/30=4 m3/s per min。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: ReleaseChangesFrom=100 to220 m3/s over30 min; meanDischargeRamp=(220-100)/30=4 m3/s per min. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「下游流量爬升」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Downstream discharge ramping\", which statement holds?","options":["平均覆土應力高就保證核心各方向應力都高","原創教學假設：ReleaseChangesFrom=100 to220 m3/s over30 min; meanDischargeRamp=(220-100)/30=4 m3/s per min。","總洩量相同就表示所有閘門組合效果相同"],"optionsEn":["High average overburden guarantees high stress in every core direction","Original teaching assumptions: ReleaseChangesFrom=100 to220 m3/s over30 min; meanDischargeRamp=(220-100)/30=4 m3/s per min.","Equal total release means every gate combination has the same effect"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：ReleaseChangesFrom=100 to220 m3/s over30 min; meanDischargeRamp=(220-100)/30=4 m3/s per min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: ReleaseChangesFrom=100 to220 m3/s over30 min; meanDischargeRamp=(220-100)/30=4 m3/s per min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b213-v15-35","title":"下游流量爬升：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Downstream discharge ramping: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「下游流量爬升」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Downstream discharge ramping” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「下游流量爬升」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Downstream discharge ramping\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","裝置容量就是任何水頭下都能維持的出力","同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Nameplate capacity is output that can be maintained at every head","Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b213-v15-36","title":"下游流量爬升：失效診斷","titleEn":"Downstream discharge ramping: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「下游流量爬升」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Downstream discharge ramping” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions. Diagnose it by the following check: Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每天總放流量相同就表示下游影響完全相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal daily release volume guarantees identical downstream effects\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions. Diagnose it by the following check: Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「下游流量爬升」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Downstream discharge ramping\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","容量因數降低就必定代表水輪機效率降低"],"optionsEn":["Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A lower capacity factor necessarily means lower turbine efficiency"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b213-v15-37","title":"枯水容量與年能量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drought capacity and annual energy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「枯水容量與年能量」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drought capacity and annual energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"枯水期間可用水量與水頭可能同時下降，使裝置容量與實際年電量差距擴大。容量因數用年能量除額定功率與時數，僅是事後或情境指標，不直接說明停機原因；需分辨水文限制、設備故障與電網需求。 驗證時應將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率，並辨識以下失效情境：容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「枯水容量與年能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"During drought both available volume and head may fall, widening the gap between capacity and energy. Capacity factor is a retrospective or scenario ratio, not a diagnosis of why output was limited. Separate hydrological constraints, equipment outages and grid demand before interpreting a lower value. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drought capacity and annual energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：HypotheticalAnnualEnergy=4200 GWh; ratedPower=1000 MW; hours=8760 h; capacityFactor=4200*1000/(1000*8760)=0.479452。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalAnnualEnergy=4200 GWh; ratedPower=1000 MW; hours=8760 h; capacityFactor=4200*1000/(1000*8760)=0.479452.","failure":"常見誤解：「容量因數降低就必定代表水輪機效率降低」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A lower capacity factor necessarily means lower turbine efficiency\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「枯水容量與年能量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drought capacity and annual energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-37-k1","title":"枯水容量與年能量","titleEn":"Drought capacity and annual energy","text":"枯水期間可用水量與水頭可能同時下降，使裝置容量與實際年電量差距擴大。容量因數用年能量除額定功率與時數，僅是事後或情境指標，不直接說明停機原因；需分辨水文限制、設備故障與電網需求。","textEn":"During drought both available volume and head may fall, widening the gap between capacity and energy. Capacity factor is a retrospective or scenario ratio, not a diagnosis of why output was limited.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：容量因數降低就必定代表水輪機效率降低 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A lower capacity factor necessarily means lower turbine efficiency Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「枯水容量與年能量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drought capacity and annual energy\" is correct?","options":["容量因數降低就必定代表水輪機效率降低","枯水期間可用水量與水頭可能同時下降，使裝置容量與實際年電量差距擴大。","所有蓄水後沉陷都只是施工壓實尚未完成"],"optionsEn":["A lower capacity factor necessarily means lower turbine efficiency","During drought both available volume and head may fall, widening the gap between capacity and energy.","Every postimpoundment settlement merely reflects unfinished construction compaction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"枯水期間可用水量與水頭可能同時下降，使裝置容量與實際年電量差距擴大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"During drought both available volume and head may fall, widening the gap between capacity and energy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b213-v15-38","title":"枯水容量與年能量：定量估算","titleEn":"Drought capacity and annual energy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「枯水容量與年能量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drought capacity and annual energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：HypotheticalAnnualEnergy=4200 GWh; ratedPower=1000 MW; hours=8760 h; capacityFactor=4200*1000/(1000*8760)=0.479452。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalAnnualEnergy=4200 GWh; ratedPower=1000 MW; hours=8760 h; capacityFactor=4200*1000/(1000*8760)=0.479452. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：HypotheticalAnnualEnergy=4200 GWh; ratedPower=1000 MW; hours=8760 h; capacityFactor=4200*1000/(1000*8760)=0.479452。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalAnnualEnergy=4200 GWh; ratedPower=1000 MW; hours=8760 h; capacityFactor=4200*1000/(1000*8760)=0.479452. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「枯水容量與年能量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drought capacity and annual energy\", which statement holds?","options":["料場試驗合格就保證每個鋪築界面都合格","閘門數量多就保證沒有任何共同失效點","原創教學假設：HypotheticalAnnualEnergy=4200 GWh; ratedPower=1000 MW; hours=8760 h; capacityFactor=4200*1000/(1000*8760)=0.479452。"],"optionsEn":["Passing stockpile tests guarantees every placed interface is acceptable","A large number of gates guarantees no common failure point","Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalAnnualEnergy=4200 GWh; ratedPower=1000 MW; hours=8760 h; capacityFactor=4200*1000/(1000*8760)=0.479452."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：HypotheticalAnnualEnergy=4200 GWh; ratedPower=1000 MW; hours=8760 h; capacityFactor=4200*1000/(1000*8760)=0.479452。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalAnnualEnergy=4200 GWh; ratedPower=1000 MW; hours=8760 h; capacityFactor=4200*1000/(1000*8760)=0.479452. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b213-v15-39","title":"枯水容量與年能量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drought capacity and annual energy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「枯水容量與年能量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drought capacity and annual energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「枯水容量與年能量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drought capacity and annual energy\"?","options":["將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","湖面積一旦量過就能固定用於所有水位"],"optionsEn":["Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","One measured lake area applies unchanged at every stage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b213-v15-40","title":"枯水容量與年能量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drought capacity and annual energy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b213-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「枯水容量與年能量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drought capacity and annual energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化。診斷時應採取以下查核：將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「容量因數降低就必定代表水輪機效率降低」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A lower capacity factor necessarily means lower turbine efficiency\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b213-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化。診斷時應採取以下查核：將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]},{"id":"b213-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「枯水容量與年能量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drought capacity and annual energy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化。","所有蓄水後沉陷都只是施工壓實尚未完成"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency.","Every postimpoundment settlement merely reflects unfinished construction compaction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-vra-akosombo","v15s-usbr-filters","v15s-hoover-owner"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
